\ The recursion from hybrid_compiled_recursion_overflow.1z, run inside a task. A task's stack is
\ its own coroutine region, so the limit compiled code checks against is the task's rather than the
\ main thread's.
\
\ Only the error type is printed, and the residue the unwound levels leave behind is wiped, since
\ the depth moves with the build.

deep: stack-recursive ( n -- n ) [ dup 0 > [ 1 - deep 1 + ] [ ] if ] ;

[ [ [ 1000000 deep drop ] [ error-type: @get . wipe ] recover ] spawn await-terminal ] task-scope
